From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 06:58:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 27/35] isolate: add feature-gated Static Hermes Wasm UDF
 execution

Add an optional runtime consumer for externally produced Static Hermes module graphs. The default backend remains V8-only unless runtime configuration, an authenticated registry, and an exact source-package binding admit a selected route.

Support independent query and mutation authority. V8-primary execution can sample a bounded Wasm shadow; Wasm-primary execution can sample a non-authoritative V8 verifier or run without a verifier. Unselected and quarantined routes remain V8-only. A successful Wasm result does not wait for V8 verification, and verifier failure, overload, timeout, cancellation, divergence, or late completion never becomes fallback or commit authority.

Bind registry generations, route leases, module contracts, context-reuse evidence, platform limits, and runtime identity to authenticated content and the pinned Wasmtime inputs. Accept directly supplied AOT artifacts and reconstruct intentionally omitted AOT from authenticated Core Wasm with the production engine before readiness. Verify reconstructed identity, preload selected graphs, retain immutable deserialization snapshots, and bound generation, module, instance, memory, and background-verifier ownership.

Add source-keyed deployment catalogs and activation records, destination readiness and lifecycle reporting, sanitized direction-specific comparison evidence, inserted-document identity normalization, failure-stage classification, and configuration validation. Preserve ordinary V8 deployment and empty-registry compatibility.

Include focused runtime and registry fixtures, generic operator documentation, source-package preactivation support, and reproducible feature-enabled self-hosted image construction.

Validation on the reviewed tree includes focused function_runner, application, isolate, local_backend, and Wasmtime deserialization tests; default application compilation; changed-file rustfmt; and git diff checks. Live image and deployment acceptance remain separate from these source checks.
